---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import SvgDefs from "../components/SvgDefs.astro"
import ThemeToggle from "../components/ThemeToggle.astro"
import Message from "../components/Message.astro"
import { loginUrl } from "../lib/config"

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "AboutPage",
    name: "About Threa",
    url: new URL("/about", Astro.site).href,
    mainEntity: {
      "@type": "Person",
      name: "Kristoffer Remback",
      sameAs: ["https://github.com/kristofferremback", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/kristofferremback/"],
    },
  },
]
---

<Layout
  title="About · Threa"
  description="Threa began as a side project, out of curiosity and frustration with workplace chat: how much more you can do with what a conversation already holds, and whether a tool like this has to lock you in. Built by Kristoffer Remback, in the open."
  schema={schema}
>
  <SvgDefs />

  <div class="about">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="hero-shell">
        <div class="hero-inner">
          <div class="nav-row" data-decorative>
            <div class="brand">
              <svg><use href="#threa-mark" /></svg>
              <span class="wordmark">Threa</span>
            </div>
            <nav class="nav-links">
              <a href="/">Product</a>
              <a href="/about" aria-current="page">About</a>
              <a href="/developers">Developers</a>
            </nav>
            <a class="nav-login" href={loginUrl}>Log in</a>
            <ThemeToggle />
          </div>

          <div class="ab-grid ab-hero">
            <h1 class="h-display">Threa came out of curiosity, and a bit of frustration.</h1>
            <p class="ab-lead">
              My day job is software engineering, where I spend a lot of time in
              tools that are <em>fine</em> but never great. The little frustrations
              add up, and eventually my curiosity got out of hand. So now
              there's this.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="frame warm ab-strands">
      <div class="memo-shell">
        <div class="ab-grid ab-intro">
          <h2>What I kept running into.</h2>
          <p class="ab-lede">
            Three of them stuck around long enough that I did something about them.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-grid ab-strand">
          <div class="ab-copy">
            <h3>What did we say again?</h3>
            <p>
              Years of decisions and their reasoning pile up in workplace chat,
              and I rarely find them again. My memory runs on gist: I'll remember
              that we discussed something, sometimes why, rarely the exact wording
              or where we said it, though I'll know it was Kate who said it. I
              started wondering whether a chat app could do something more useful
              with all that conversational data, keeping decisions and their
              reasoning tied to the messages they came from. I assumed it would
              cost too much. So far it hasn't.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="ab-scene ab-scene-kept" data-decorative aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="recall-meta"><span class="hash">#api-v3</span><span>Mar 12</span></div>
            <Message author="jordan" time="11:42">
              <div class="tl-text">hold on, I'm not comfortable changing the auth boundary without working through the token-rotation flow first. can we pause this?</div>
            </Message>
            <Message author="maya" time="11:44">
              <div class="tl-text">Fair. Let's hold v3 until you've walked us through it.</div>
            </Message>
            <p class="ab-kept">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9.937 15.5A2 2 0 0 0 8.5 14.063l-6.135-1.582a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.962L8.5 9.936A2 2 0 0 0 9.937 8.5l1.582-6.135a.5.5 0 0 1 .963 0L14.063 8.5A2 2 0 0 0 15.5 9.937l6.135 1.581a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .964L15.5 14.063a2 2 0 0 0-1.437 1.437l-1.582 6.135a.5.5 0 0 1-.963 0z" /><path d="M20 3v4M22 5h-4M4 17v2M5 18H3" /></svg>
              Saved to memory: <span class="ab-kept-title">Auth refactor held pending token-rotation review</span>
            </p>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-grid ab-strand is-flipped">
          <div class="ab-copy">
            <h3>Tools are supposed to be yours.</h3>
            <p>
              Most tools want to become the platform you can't afford to leave, and
              lately plenty of them insist on shipping their own AI agent. I rarely
              want it. The agent I already use has my codebase, my tools, and the
              context I've built around it. Another agent inside another app starts
              without them. Threa has Ariadne too, and I want her to be genuinely
              great, but she's at her best inside the room, where the shared context
              lives. For my own work I'd rather bring the agent I already use, so
              Threa connects to it through the bot runtime, public API, CLI, and MCP
              server instead of trying to replace it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="ab-scene" data-decorative aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="recall-meta"><span class="hash">#api-v3</span><span>Apr 20</span></div>
            <Message author="alex" time="16:20">
              <div class="tl-text"><span class="mention">@claude-code</span> does the rotation fix cover mobile sessions too?</div>
            </Message>
            <Message author="claude-code" time="16:21">
              <div class="tl-text">Not yet. The migration in rotation.ts only moves web refresh tokens. I've started on mobile in <span class="ref-pill">auth-rotation</span>.</div>
            </Message>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-grid ab-strand">
          <div class="ab-copy">
            <h3>Chat could be so much nicer.</h3>
            <p>
              Nested threading, quoting, replying to one message in a busy room,
              formatting that behaves. None of it sells a platform, which is
              probably why it keeps getting skipped, but it all adds up over a day
              spent in chat. After years of putting up with the basics done badly,
              I think we deserve nice things.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="ab-scene" data-decorative aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="recall-meta"><span class="hash">#product</span><span>May 7</span></div>
            <Message author="jordan" time="10:02" class="ab-noise">
              <div class="tl-text">standup moved to 10:30 btw</div>
            </Message>
            <Message author="sam" time="10:03" class="ab-noise">
              <div class="tl-text">pizza again on friday? taking orders</div>
            </Message>
            <Message author="maya" time="10:04">
              <div class="quote-card">
                <div class="qm"><svg><use href="#quote-icon" /></svg></div>
                <div class="q-author">
                  <div class="q-avatar tl-avatar av-sam">SP</div>
                  <div class="q-name">Sam Patel</div>
                  <div class="q-time">09:41</div>
                </div>
                <div class="q-body">empty states for the board are on staging now</div>
              </div>
              <div class="tl-text ab-after">These look great. Can they ship with v3 on Thursday?</div>
              <div class="reactions"><span class="rxn"><span class="em">🙌</span><span class="num">2</span></span></div>
            </Message>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="frame">
      <div class="memo-shell">
        <div class="ab-grid ab-team">
          <div class="ab-letter">
            <h2>I'm the team.</h2>
            <p>
              Hi, I'm Kristoffer. People have paid me to build software for over ten
              years now. During parental leave I started tinkering on Threa to keep
              myself from going insane, and I'm not sure it worked: here I am, up late
              after my wife has gone to bed, talking to an agent about who I am and why
              I'm building this.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="ab-sig">
            <div class="ab-sig-who" data-decorative aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="ab-sig-mark">KR</span>
              <span class="ab-sig-name">Kristoffer Remback</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ab-links">
              <a href="https://github.com/kristofferremback" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
              <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kristofferremback/" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="frame">
      <div class="memo-shell ab-principles-shell">
        <div class="ab-grid ab-principles">
          <div class="ab-stance">
            <h2>Built the way I want tools to work.</h2>
            <p>
              Good at its job, composable with everything else, and easy to step away
              from. Threa is built that way on purpose. The door stays open, so if you
              stay it's because you want to, not because leaving would cost you.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="ab-practice">
            <p class="ab-lede">
              It has also been my way into building with AI agents. Most of Threa is
              written by directing them, but the thinking stays mine, and that matters
              more than ever. They're a good way to chase a curiosity, and you can get
              genuinely decent software out of them as long as you do the thinking
              yourself. Seeing where they shine and where they fall short has been half
              the fun. It's a work in progress, on what I think is a good trajectory.
              The repo is public, so have a look.
            </p>
            <div class="ab-links">
              <a href="https://github.com/threahq/threa">Browse the source on GitHub</a>
              <a href="/developers/feature-requests">Request a feature</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="frame night">
      <div class="memo-shell ab-close">
        <div class="ab-grid">
          <h2>Early, and built in the open.</h2>
          <div>
            <p class="ab-lede">
              Threa is early, and there's plenty left to build. Join the waitlist, or
              follow along in the public repo.
            </p>
            <a class="cta" href="/#waitlist">Join the waitlist</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <footer class="footer">
      <div class="brand" style="gap:10px;">
        <svg style="width:24px;height:24px;color:hsl(var(--gold));"><use href="#threa-mark" /></svg>
        <span class="wordmark" style="font-size:18px;">Threa</span>
        <span class="year">2026</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ln">
        <a href="/">Product</a>
        <a href="/about">About</a>
        <a href="/developers">Developers</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    /* The page's one moment: when the first scene scrolls into view, the two
       source messages glow and the memory line lands under them, the way the app
       marks a capture. Without the observer, or with reduced motion, the scene
       is simply shown finished. */
    (function () {
      const scene = document.querySelector(".ab-scene-kept")
      if (!scene || !("IntersectionObserver" in window)) return
      if (matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) return
      scene.classList.add("is-waiting")
      const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        if (!entries.some((e) => e.isIntersecting)) return
        io.disconnect()
        scene.classList.add("is-kept")
      }, { threshold: 0.8 })
      io.observe(scene)
    })()
  </script>

  <style>
    /* One knob for every display heading on this page, so the site-wide
       weight can be tried here without touching global.css. */
    .about {
      --about-display-weight: 600;
    }

    /* A 12-column grid shared by every section. Headings and the left copy
       start at column 1, the right copy at column 7, so sections change shape
       without changing axes. */
    .ab-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
      column-gap: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 32px);
    }

    .hero-shell::before { display: none; }
    .ab-hero .h-display {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      font-weight: var(--about-display-weight);
      font-size: clamp(42px, 6.6vw, 96px);
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      line-height: 1;
      text-wrap: balance;
      margin: 0 0 44px;
    }
    .ab-lead {
      grid-column: 7 / -1;
      margin: 0;
      max-width: 32em;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
    }

    .about .memo-shell h2 {
      font-weight: var(--about-display-weight);
      letter-spacing: -0.022em;
      line-height: 1.06;
      text-wrap: balance;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .ab-lede {
      margin: 0;
      text-wrap: pretty;
      max-width: 36em;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: hsl(var(--ink-soft));
    }

    .ab-intro { align-items: baseline; }
    .ab-intro h2 { grid-column: 1 / span 5; }
    .ab-intro .ab-lede { grid-column: 7 / -1; }

    /* The three strands mirror each other: copy left and scene right, then
       swapped, then back, around the same two axes. */
    .ab-strand {
      margin-top: clamp(72px, 9vw, 120px);
      align-items: center;
    }
    .ab-intro + .ab-strand { margin-top: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px); }
    .ab-strand .ab-copy { grid-column: 1 / span 6; grid-row: 1; }
    .ab-strand .ab-scene { grid-column: 8 / -1; grid-row: 1; }
    .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-copy { grid-column: 7 / -1; }
    .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-scene { grid-column: 1 / span 5; }

    .ab-copy h3 {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: var(--about-display-weight);
      font-size: clamp(24px, 2.5vw, 32px);
      line-height: 1.1;
      letter-spacing: -0.018em;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
      text-wrap: balance;
    }
    .ab-copy p {
      margin: 0;
      text-wrap: pretty;
      max-width: 34em;
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.65;
      color: hsl(var(--ink-soft));
    }

    /* Each scene is a strip of the app sliding in from the page edge: a
       paper panel that bleeds off the side it sits on, alternating with the
       strands so the section swings instead of leaning. */
    .about .ab-strands { overflow-x: clip; }
    .about .ab-strands .memo-shell { overflow: visible; }
    .ab-scene {
      position: relative;
      isolation: isolate;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 18px 0 22px;
    }
    .ab-scene::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      z-index: -1;
      inset: 0 -100vw 0 -24px;
      background: hsl(var(--paper));
      border: 1px solid hsl(var(--line));
      border-right: 0;
      border-radius: 16px 0 0 16px;
    }
    .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-scene::before {
      inset: 0 -24px 0 -100vw;
      border: 1px solid hsl(var(--line));
      border-left: 0;
      border-radius: 0 16px 16px 0;
    }
    .ab-scene .recall-meta { padding: 0 12px; margin-bottom: 2px; }
    .ab-scene :global(.tl-row.ab-noise) { opacity: 0.42; }
    .ab-scene .quote-card { margin: 6px 0 8px; }
    .ab-after { margin-top: 2px; }

    .ab-kept {
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0 6px;
      margin: 14px 0 0;
      padding: 0 12px;
      font-size: 13.5px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      text-align: center;
      color: hsl(var(--muted));
    }
    .ab-kept svg {
      flex: none;
      width: 14px;
      height: 14px;
      align-self: center;
      color: hsl(var(--gold));
    }
    .ab-kept-title {
      font-weight: 500;
      color: hsl(var(--ink) / 0.8);
    }

    .ab-scene-kept.is-waiting .ab-kept {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(6px);
    }
    .ab-scene-kept.is-kept .ab-kept {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
      transition: opacity 0.5s ease-out 1.1s, transform 0.5s ease-out 1.1s;
    }
    .ab-scene-kept.is-kept .ab-kept svg {
      animation: kept-spark 0.7s ease-out 1.1s both;
    }
    .ab-scene-kept.is-kept :global(.tl-row) {
      animation: kept-glow 2.4s ease-in-out 0.2s both;
    }
    @keyframes kept-glow {
      0%, 100% { background-color: hsl(var(--gold) / 0); }
      30%, 55% { background-color: hsl(var(--gold) / 0.12); }
    }
    @keyframes kept-spark {
      from { transform: scale(0.4) rotate(-40deg); }
      to { transform: none; }
    }

    /* The team section reads as a note: the heading runs into the paragraph
       at reading size across most of the width, signed off in the margin. */
    .ab-team { align-items: end; }
    .ab-letter { grid-column: 1 / span 8; }
    .about .ab-letter h2,
    .ab-letter p {
      display: inline;
      font-size: clamp(22px, 2.3vw, 30px);
      line-height: 1.45;
    }
    .about .ab-letter h2 {
      margin-right: 0.15em;
      letter-spacing: -0.012em;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
    }
    .ab-letter p {
      margin: 0;
      color: hsl(var(--ink-soft));
    }
    .ab-sig { grid-column: 10 / -1; }
    .ab-sig-who {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px;
    }
    .ab-sig-mark {
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      flex: none;
      width: 44px;
      height: 44px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: hsl(var(--gold) / 0.16);
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: var(--about-display-weight);
      font-size: 16px;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }
    .ab-sig-name {
      font-size: 15px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
    }
    .ab-sig .ab-links { margin-top: 20px; }

    /* Principles share the page's plain paper with the team note; a rule and
       a heading set at the page's second size mark the turn instead of a
       tint. */
    .about .ab-principles-shell { padding-top: 0; }
    .ab-principles {
      align-items: start;
      padding-top: clamp(64px, 7vw, 96px);
      border-top: 1px solid hsl(var(--line));
    }
    .ab-stance { display: contents; }
    .about .ab-principles h2 {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      grid-row: 1;
      max-width: none;
      margin-bottom: clamp(32px, 4vw, 56px);
      font-size: clamp(36px, 4.6vw, 64px);
      letter-spacing: -0.028em;
      line-height: 1.02;
    }
    .ab-stance p {
      grid-column: 1 / span 5;
      grid-row: 2;
      margin: 0;
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: clamp(20px, 1.9vw, 24px);
      line-height: 1.35;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
    }
    .ab-practice { grid-column: 7 / -1; grid-row: 2; }
    .ab-practice .ab-lede { padding-top: 4px; }

    .ab-links {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 12px 28px;
      margin-top: 26px;
    }
    .ab-links a {
      font-size: 15px;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-decoration-color: hsl(var(--gold) / 0.5);
      text-underline-offset: 4px;
    }
    .ab-links a:focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid hsl(var(--gold));
      outline-offset: 3px;
      border-radius: 2px;
    }

    /* The close takes the home page's night register, so both pages end on
       the same weight. */
    .ab-close .ab-grid { align-items: baseline; }
    .ab-close .ab-grid > :first-child { grid-column: 1 / span 5; }
    .ab-close .ab-grid > :last-child { grid-column: 7 / -1; }
    .about .ab-close h2 { color: hsl(38 16% 94%); }
    .ab-close .ab-lede { color: hsl(35 12% 72%); margin-bottom: 28px; }

    @media (hover: hover) {
      .ab-links a:hover { text-decoration-color: hsl(var(--gold)); }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .ab-scene-kept .ab-kept,
      .ab-scene-kept .ab-kept svg,
      .ab-scene-kept :global(.tl-row) {
        opacity: 1;
        transform: none;
        animation: none;
        transition: none;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 880px) {
      .ab-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
      .ab-grid > *,
      .ab-hero .h-display,
      .ab-intro h2,
      .ab-intro .ab-lede,
      .ab-letter,
      .ab-sig,
      .ab-strand .ab-copy,
      .ab-strand .ab-scene,
      .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-copy,
      .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-scene,
      .ab-close .ab-grid > :first-child,
      .ab-close .ab-grid > :last-child,
      .about .ab-principles h2,
      .ab-stance p,
      .ab-practice {
        grid-column: 1;
        grid-row: auto;
      }
      .ab-hero .h-display { margin-bottom: 24px; }
      .ab-lead { font-size: 18px; }
      .ab-lede { font-size: 17px; }
      .about .ab-intro h2,
      .about .ab-close h2 { margin-bottom: 16px; }
      .ab-strand { margin-top: 64px; }
      .ab-intro + .ab-strand { margin-top: 48px; }
      .ab-strand .ab-scene { margin-top: 28px; }
      .ab-scene::before,
      .ab-strand.is-flipped .ab-scene::before {
        inset: 0 -100vw;
        border-left: 0;
        border-right: 0;
        border-radius: 0;
      }
      .ab-copy h3 { margin-bottom: 10px; }
      .ab-copy p { font-size: 16px; }
      .ab-practice { margin-top: 28px; }
      .ab-sig { margin-top: 36px; }
      .ab-practice .ab-lede { padding-top: 0; }
    }

    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .about .memo-shell { padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 64px; }
      .ab-scene .recall-meta { padding: 0; }
      .ab-scene :global(.tl-row) { padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; }
      .ab-scene :global(.tl-row.bot) { padding-left: 10px; }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
